You feel spoiled.

	The first thing you want to do what identifying any sort of item is to
determine whether the item is blessed or cursed.  There are a couple of ways
to figure this out.  One is to remember that your pet will not step on a pile
containing a cursed item, or at least will be very reluctant to do so.
Another is to drop the item in question on an altar.  This will tell you for
certain the blessed/cursed status of the item.  Once you have determined your
potion or scroll is not cursed, the only way to learn anything more about its
effects is to use it.  When reading unidentified scrolls, be prepared for
scrolls of fire, destroy armor, and amnesia.  Scrolls of punishment aren't
very friendly, either, but they're almost impossible to prepare for.

>Also, if I get 'deathly sick', can I do anything to prevent dying?

	You could #pray, a)pply a unicorn horn, or q)uaff a potion of extra
healing.

